INT. WITHERED SALON IN A CLOSED CHATEAU - 1789 - NIGHT

A great room under dust sheets. A single candle burns on a harpsichord whose lid has been propped open with a book. Shuttered windows. Outside, far off, a crowd murmurs like the sea.

An old woman, MADAME HORTENSE DE VALLOMBREUSE-ADEYEMI (70s, silver silk gone gray at the hem, a ring on every finger), sits at the harpsichord. She does not play. She presses one key, listens to its fading note, and presses another.

The door opens. A young man slips in and shuts it behind him, breathing hard. LOUIS-MARIE FONTAINE-OKOYE (20s, servant's livery, torn collar, a candle stub in his hand) is the last of her household.

HORTENSE
You are late, Louis-Marie.

LOUIS-MARIE
Madame, the gates are down. They are in the courtyard.

HORTENSE
I heard.

LOUIS-MARIE
Then you must come. There is a cart in the stable. I have bribed the boy.

HORTENSE
With what?

LOUIS-MARIE
With your emeralds.

HORTENSE
Ah. Those were never mine.

LOUIS-MARIE
Madame, please.

She presses a key. The note hangs.

HORTENSE
Do you know, I have lived in this house for fifty-one years and never once been alone in this room. There was always someone to carry a candle. Someone to close a shutter. Someone to watch me not play.

LOUIS-MARIE
I am here.

HORTENSE
Yes. You are the last.

LOUIS-MARIE
Madame, they will burn it.

HORTENSE
I should hope so. It is a great deal of work to maintain.

He kneels beside the stool. She does not look at him. The crowd's murmur swells into a roar and the candle on the harpsichord gutters.

LOUIS-MARIE
Please. For my sake.

HORTENSE
Then do this for mine. Take the candle. Go through the kitchen. Do not look back, and do not tell them you served me.

LOUIS-MARIE
They will know.

HORTENSE
They will know that you ran. That is enough.

She finally turns. Touches his face with a ringed hand, once, lightly.

HORTENSE (CONT'D)
Go.

He rises. Backs away. At the door he stops, then bows low, deeper than any servant should. The door closes. She turns back to the keys and plays, at last, one slow chord that fills the dark room.
